# ZvenFit — core rules

Static site built by Astro into `dist/`: pages in `src/pages`, shared markup in
`src/layouts` and `src/components`, data in `src/content` and `src/data`, classic
browser scripts in `src/scripts`, static files copied as they are in `public/`. No
client framework on pages (an island needs a justification in the PR). Do not assume
React or Next.

The site is built by Astro since release A (plan `docs/astro-migration.md`, ADR
`knowledge-base/decisions/002-astro-migration.md`): every route comes from Astro sources
(20 pages in `src/pages`, 21 trainer pages from `src/content/trainers/*.json`). The
legacy build (`scripts/build-static.cjs`, `scripts/snippets/`, the pages, styles and
scripts of `public/`) is no longer in the tree; it exists only in git history, last in
`d5aeb4a` (`v3.1.4`). Release A was accepted on 2026-11-17, and the converter of the
migration and the `compare-dist` job are removed: pages, trainer entries, stylesheets and
browser scripts are edited by hand like any other source, and no check compares the built
site with an earlier one. A change that must not alter the site is proven by two builds
with the same variables and `diff -r` of the two `dist/` (see `AGENTS.md`, Verification).
Never put a file into `public/` at the path of a route: Astro ships it instead of the
page or the endpoint.
Source: `src/`, `public/`, `scripts/`, `functions/`. **Never edit `dist/` or `.astro/`.**

After changes: `npm run build` or `npm run dev`; verify with `npm run check`,
`npm run lint`, `npm run test:build`. `npm run compare:dist` is a manual tool kept for
release B; no job runs it.

## APIs (endpoints built from env)

- Lead: `functions/lead-intake/` → `src/pages/js/lead-config.js.ts` → `window.ZVENFIT_LEAD_API`
- Schedule: `functions/fitbase-schedule/` → `src/pages/js/schedule-config.js.ts` → `window.ZVENFIT_SCHEDULE_API`
- Page views: `functions/site-traffic/` → `src/pages/js/traffic-config.js.ts` → `window.ZVENFIT_TRAFFIC_API`

## Shared markup

Menu, footer, analytics, Open Graph, JSON-LD and app badges are components in
`src/components/` rendered by `src/layouts/Base.astro`. Their whitespace reproduces
the legacy pages and no check guards it any more: Prettier is off for `src/layouts`,
`src/components` and `src/pages`, do not reformat them. Comments inside component
children are dropped by the compiler (use `set:html`), raw non-breaking spaces become
plain spaces (use `&nbsp;`).

## Brand

Keep green `#00d10e`, Roadrage + Roboto. See `TODO.md` "Out of scope".

## Secrets

No tokens in HTML/JS. Use env / GitHub Secrets only.

## Deploy

**Frontend (`zvenfit-frontend` bucket):** only via GitHub Actions (`.github/workflows/main.yml`).
Do **not** manually upload to `zvenfit-frontend` (`yc storage s3api put-object`, `aws s3 cp/sync` towards the bucket, etc.) unless the user explicitly asks. `scripts/snapshot-bucket.sh` only downloads; the owner runs it with their own credentials.

A push to `main` starts a release: staging deploy and E2E first, then production (`npm run build`, `s3 sync ./dist`). Work on a branch and open a pull request. A rollback is a `git revert` pull request through the same release (`knowledge-base/staging-runbook.md`, "Frontend rollback").

**Assets bucket (`zvenfit`):** coach images and static CDN assets — not deployed by CI; manual ops only when the user requests or approves.
